  "body": {
    "id": "thm:feasible-window-wald",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every sequence in \\(\\mathcal P_n\\), including sequences with \\(H\\to\\infty\\), \\(\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{bc}}-\\tau=-L+o_{\\mathbb P}(s)\\), \\(\\widehat V/s^2\\to_{\\mathbb P}1\\), and the primitive conditional block-dependence and score-diffuseness conditions yield \\(\\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal P_n}\\sup_{z\\in\\mathbb R}|\\mathbb P_P\\{(\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{bc}}-\\tau)/\\sqrt{\\widehat V}\\le z\\mid M,\\Omega\\}-\\Phi(z)|\\to0\\). Consequently, \\(\\inf_{P\\in\\mathcal P_n}\\mathbb P_P\\{\\tau\\in\\mathrm{CI}_{1-\\alpha}\\mid M,\\Omega\\}\\to1-\\alpha\\). This strictly extends Choi and Yuan (2024), Theorem 3.1, for the same native subgroup estimator from \\(q=0,H=1\\) to fixed \\(q\\ge1\\), growing \\(H\\), and a feasible nonzero curvature correction.",
