    "justification": "Native expansion, feasible curvature correction, covariance consistency, and fitted-weight stability turn the oracle score limit into implementable sustained-effect inference.",
    "gap": "Prior one-date completion and missing-factor HAC results do not give this corrected growing-window law for the native estimator.",
    "consumer": "The interval supports a scalar reanalysis of the SEC Tick Size Pilot's average sustained liquidity effect over the realized cohort and post window.",
    "proof_tex": "On \\(G\\times W\\), the common-start mask gives \\(A_{it}=1\\), so causal consistency gives \\(Y^{\\mathrm{obs}}_{it}=Y_{it}(1)\\). Comparing the definitions of the causal target and estimator therefore gives the exact, observed-law-to-causal relation\n\\[\n \\widehat\\tau-\\tau\n =-\\frac1{gH}\\sum_{i\\in G,t\\in W}(\\widehat M_{it}-M_{it}).\n\\tag{59}\n\\]\nThis equality is derived from consistency and the untreated factor model; it is not part of the definition of the causal effect. By the native-transfer theorem and \\(\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{bc}}=\\widehat\\tau+\\widehat B_2\\),\n\\[\n \\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{bc}}-\\tau\n =-L-(Q-B_2)-R_{\\mathrm{agg}}+(\\widehat B_2-B_2)\n =-L+o_{\\mathbb P}(s),\n\\tag{60}\n\\]\nuniformly over \\(\\mathcal P_n\\).\n\nFor variance consistency, let \\(d=\\widehat w-w\\), and let \\(\\Gamma_q\\) and \\(\\widehat\\Gamma_q\\) be the banded Toeplitz matrices with entries\n\\[\n (\\Gamma_q)_{uv}=1\\{|u-v|\\le q\\}\\gamma(v-u),\n \\qquad\n (\\widehat\\Gamma_q)_{uv}=1\\{|u-v|\\le q\\}\\widehat\\gamma(v-u).\n\\]\nThe two variance definitions give\n\\[\n s^2=\\sum_jw_{j\\cdot}^{\\top}\\Gamma_qw_{j\\cdot},\n \\qquad\n \\widehat V=\\sum_j(w_{j\\cdot}+d_{j\\cdot})^{\\top}\n \\widehat\\Gamma_q(w_{j\\cdot}+d_{j\\cdot}).\n\\tag{61}\n\\]\nFixed \\(q\\), the moment bound, and covariance consistency imply\n\\[\n \\|\\widehat\\Gamma_q\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}=O_{\\mathbb P}(1),\n \\qquad\n \\|\\widehat\\Gamma_q-\\Gamma_q\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\n \\le(2q+1)\\Delta_\\gamma=o_{\\mathbb P}(1).\n\\tag{62}\n\\]\nExpanding (61), applying Cauchy--Schwarz, and using \\(\\|w\\|_F^2=O(s^2)\\) from the established score-diffuseness lemma and \\(\\|d\\|_F^2=o_{\\mathbb P}(s^2)\\) from native transfer, gives\n\\[\n \\frac{|\\widehat V-s^2|}{s^2}\n \\le O_{\\mathbb P}(1)\\left\\{\n \\frac{2\\|w\\|_F\\|d\\|_F+\\|d\\|_F^2}{s^2}\n +\\Delta_\\gamma\\frac{\\|w\\|_F^2}{s^2}\\right\\}\n =o_{\\mathbb P}(1).\n\\tag{63}\n\\]\nVariance nondegeneracy makes \\(s^2>0\\), and (63) also implies \\(\\widehat V>0\\) with probability tending uniformly to one.\n\nThe established conditional score central limit theorem applies to \\(L/s\\). Normal symmetry gives the same limit for \\(-L/s\\). Equations (60), (63), and conditional Slutsky therefore yield\n\\[\n \\sup_{P\\in\\mathcal P_n}\\sup_{z\\in\\mathbb R}\n \\left|\\mathbb P_P\\!\\left\\{\n \\frac{\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{bc}}-\\tau}{\\sqrt{\\widehat V}}\n \\le z\\,\\middle|\\,M,\\Omega\\right\\}-\\Phi(z)\\right|\\longrightarrow0.\n\\tag{64}\n\\]\nEvaluating (64) at the two continuity points \\(\\pm z_{1-\\alpha/2}\\), for fixed \\(\\alpha\\in(0,1)\\), proves\n\\[\n \\inf_{P\\in\\mathcal P_n}\n \\mathbb P_P\\{\\tau\\in\\mathrm{CI}_{1-\\alpha}\\mid M,\\Omega\\}\n \\longrightarrow1-\\alpha.\n\\]\nThe argument is scalar and applies to a declared consecutive window, including \\(H\\to\\infty\\); it makes no assertion about simultaneous event-time bands, unknown rank, or the proportional-window noise-boundary regime.",
